.TH BIFROST-EMU 1 "November 2026" "bifrost-emu 2.0.0-beta.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bifrost-emu \- run AArch64 Linux programs and Android apps on x86-64
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bifrost-emu
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIPROGRAM\fR [\fIARGUMENT\fR]...
.br
.B bifrost-emu \-\-setup\-rootfs
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs an AArch64 Linux ELF program, translating it to x86-64 as it runs. Statically linked programs need
nothing else. Dynamically linked programs need a guest root filesystem, found automatically next to the
executable, in the user's data directory or system-wide; create one with \fB\-\-setup\-rootfs\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-setup\-rootfs [\-\-system | \-\-prefix DIR | \-\-full | \-\-profile NAME | \-\-games | \-\-uninstall]
Download the glibc and musl toolchains (about 235 MB) and install a guest rootfs, then exit.
\fB\-\-games\fR adds the libraries Linux games need as profile "games". Android apps use neither: Asgard brings its own.
.TP
.BI \-\-rootfs " PATH"
Use PATH as the guest's root: libraries come from it and guest paths are confined to it.
.TP
.BI \-\-rootfs\-profile " NAME"
Use the installed rootfs profile NAME for libraries only.
.TP
.BI \-\-rootfs\-default " NAME"
Save NAME as the profile to use from now on, in your own config file, and exit. "default" goes back to the normal rootfs.
.TP
.B \-\-rootfs\-list
List the installed rootfs profiles; the one in use is marked with an asterisk.
.TP
.B \-\-guest\-ld
Run dynamically linked programs under the rootfs's own dynamic linker (experimental).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-jit
Use the interpreter only.
.TP
.B \-\-jit
Use the JIT. This is the default.
.TP
.BI \-\-jit\-threshold " N"
Interpret for N instructions, then switch to the JIT.
.TP
.B \-\-jit\-disk\-cache[=verify]
Experimental: reuse JIT translations across launches. The cache is under \fI$XDG_CACHE_HOME/bifrost/jit\fR (or \fI~/.cache/bifrost/jit\fR), limited per application by \fBBIFROST_JIT_DISK_CACHE_MB\fR (default 512).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-jit\-disk\-cache
Do not use that cache.
.TP
.B \-\-window\-stats
Show presentation statistics (off by default): frames per second, CPU, GPU and memory, in the window title and an overlay.
.TP
.BI \-\-window\-stats\-mode " MODE"
1 or minimal: title only; 2 or normal: title and overlay; 3: overlay only. Turns the statistics on.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-window\-stats
Turn every statistics display off.
.TP
.B \-\-render\-log\fR, \fB\-\-no\-render\-log
Log the first frame presented (on by default).
.TP
.B \-\-raw\-tty
Force raw terminal input: per character, no echo.
.TP
.BI \-\-android " PATH"
Run a NativeActivity shared object (\fBANativeActivity_onCreate\fR). Apps installed with Asgard are started with \fBasgard\fR instead.
.TP
.B \-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug
Trace every instruction to standard error.
.TP
.B \-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose
Print execution statistics on exit.
.TP
.B \-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet
Suppress BRK warnings, even with \fB\-d\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-fb\-dump " PATH"
Dump \fI/dev/fb0\fR to PATH on exit (PPM).
.TP
.BI \-\-audio\-dump " PATH"
Dump \fI/dev/dsp\fR to PATH on exit (WAV).
.TP
.B \-\-print\-config
Print the resolved configuration and exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read the configuration from PATH. A sample is in /usr/share/doc/bifrost\-emu/examples/.
.TP
.B \-V\fR, \fB\-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h\fR, \fB\-\-help
Print the options and exit. With no arguments at all, bifrost-emu prints a short
page: how to run something, what is installed, and the command for what is missing.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Print the options, including those Asgard uses internally, and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BIFROST_ROOT
Same as \fB\-\-rootfs\fR.
.TP
.B BIFROST_ROOTFS_PROFILE
Same as \fB\-\-rootfs\-profile\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bifrost/rootfs
The default guest rootfs; named profiles are in \fI~/.local/share/bifrost/rootfs.d/\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/bifrost/setup
Working copy of the setup scripts, with the downloaded toolchains.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project documentation in /usr/share/doc/bifrost\-emu/ and https://github.com/sloppyman2567/bifrost\-emu.
